{"evt":"summary_set","id":"note:note-mqqv4ix36dd","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","summary":"SPEC IS INCOMPLETE: the /subconscious/search-context event-loop wedge was NOT slowness in buildGraph or embed — it was a rerank sidecar cold-start spawn storm. The multi-round agentic search-context loop (lib/subconscious/index.js runAgenticContextSearches) calls the cross-encoder rerank() once per round (rerank is ON by default in memory-search.js). rerank's sidecar is spawned lazily on first call; the child writes its PID file only after Node boots + server.listen fires, and its unix-socket/named-pipe does not accept until the ~80MB cross-encoder finishes loading (seconds). The old spawnSidecar() guard deduped solely on the PID file, so EVERY rerank() failure during that cold window spawned ANOTHER sidecar. A few back-to-back search-context calls (each several rounds) detonated one cold start into N concurrent model-loading processes that saturated the CPU and starved the daemon's own event loop — /health stopped responding and later calls hung past their socket timeout (event-loop block, not slowness). Onboard was unaffected because it uses the eagerly-spawned EMBED sidecar (single instance), not lazy rerank. Fix: in-process spawn cooldown latch (_lastSpawnAt/SPAWN_COOLDOWN_MS=30s) in lib/rerank.js AND lib/embed.js caps spawns to one per cooldown regardless of PID-file timing; plus server.on('error') EADDRINUSE guard in lib/rerank-server.js + lib/embed-server.js so a bind-race loser exits before loading a model; rerank-server no longer unconditionally unlinks a live winner socket. Regression: test/subconscious-search-context-wedge.test.js (24-call rerank burst spawns at most once; 6 rapid search-context calls keep a 25ms event-loop probe responsive). Implication for task #4 (adding an LLM call into this same loop): any new per-round sidecar/subprocess MUST carry the same single-spawn cooldown discipline or it will reintroduce the wedge.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-23T16:33:09.793Z"}
